      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Normally an increase in lung deposition leads to an improved clinical effect. An increase in clinical effect should be substantial (two-fold or greater) in order to be detected even in carefully conducted clinical trials. Further studies are needed in order to define the best clinical study designs with which to detect differences between different inhalers."},
